            <fr:title text="The categorical logician">The categorical logician</fr:title>
            <fr:taxon>Audience</fr:taxon>
          </fr:frontmatter>
          <fr:mainmatter>
            <html:p>The <html:strong>categorical logician</html:strong> is a reader who is comfortable with modern approaches to the categorical semantics of type theory, such as:</html:p>
            <html:ul><html:li><fr:link href="/shulman-2016-categorical/" title="Categorical logic from a categorical point of view" uri="https://coln-project.github.io/shulman-2016-categorical/" display-uri="shulman-2016-categorical" type="local">Categorical logic from a categorical point of view</fr:link></html:li>
  <html:li><fr:link href="/kovacs-2022-typetheoretic/" title="Type-Theoretic Signatures for Algebraic
Theories and Inductive Types" uri="https://coln-project.github.io/kovacs-2022-typetheoretic/" display-uri="kovacs-2022-typetheoretic" type="local">Type-Theoretic Signatures for Algebraic
Theories and Inductive Types</fr:link></html:li>
  <html:li><fr:link href="/uemura-2021-abstract/" title="Abstract and Concrete Type Theories" uri="https://coln-project.github.io/uemura-2021-abstract/" display-uri="uemura-2021-abstract" type="local">Abstract and Concrete Type Theories</fr:link></html:li></html:ul>
            <html:p>The categorical logician also has a reasonable grasp of topos theory and 2-category theory.</html:p>
          </fr:mainmatter>
